# Shell scripts keep LF on every checkout.
#
# The windows-latest runner checks out with core.autocrlf=true, which
# rewrites LF to CRLF. bash — Git Bash included — reads the CR as part of
# each command (`$'\r': command not found`), so a CRLF shell script is a
# broken one. It also broke a test: shared_memory::guard reads
# scripts/repo-invariants.sh and asserts it carries, byte for byte, the
# block its spec renders, which a CRLF copy never does (2026-09-18).
*.sh text eol=lf
scripts/pre-push text eol=lf

# ES-module scripts keep LF too. Several start with a `#!/usr/bin/env node`
# shebang, and under Vitest a CRLF copy fails to load at all
# ("SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token"), so on a Windows checkout
# scripts/check-envvar-layout.test.mjs reported a broken suite while the
# same file passed with LF (2026-10-08).
*.mjs text eol=lf

# Generated artefacts that a gate compares byte for byte keep LF too.
# scripts/build-cc-env-spec.py --check (run by verify-docs) reads
# cc-env-spec.json in binary mode and compares it with the LF text it
# generates, so a CRLF checkout failed the gate on every Windows clone
# (2026-10-08).
crates/claudepot-core/data/cc-env-spec.json text eol=lf
